    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174-a1">

                <pb facs="0307" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Lord Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 28, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to transmit a copy of
                    a letter received from Messrs. Duncan, Squarey &amp; Blackmore, to whom I have
                    referred for advice in regard to my response to the inquiry which your lordship
                    did me the honor to address to me on the 23d instant, together with the
                    enclosure therein. I am led to the conclusion, for the reasons given in this
                    letter, that it would not be advisable now to propose, on the part of my
                    government, to take an active part in the prosecutions connected with the
                    Alexandra. I am the more confirmed in this opinion from the fact that I have
                    reason soon to expect more specific directions from Washington in connexion with
                    the management of the questions involved in the proceedings that may be taken in
                    the courts.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d174-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d174-a1-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
